# Jekyll GitHub Pages site

This repository is the **Timberline Blazers Booster Club** public site. Do not follow parent `AL Projects` AL, Object ID, AL-Go, or Object ID Ninja rules. Never run `Pull-CursorRules.ps1` in this repo.

## Stack

- GitHub Pages **native Jekyll** via the `github-pages` gem (not Jekyll 4, not a custom Actions build).
- Theme: **Minima**. Layouts: `home`, `page`, `post`, plus `_layouts/menu.html` for QR menus.
- Allowed plugins in `_config.yml`: `jekyll-feed`, `jekyll-seo-tag`, `jekyll-sitemap`. Prefer other **github-pages whitelist** plugins (`jekyll-redirect-from`) over custom Ruby gems.
- Live host: **https://timberlineblazerboosters.org** (`CNAME`). Keep `url` in `_config.yml` matching that host so canonicals, `jekyll-seo-tag`, and `/feed.xml` are correct.

## Content model

- Nav: `_config.yml` `header_pages`. Do not add `/compose/` or `/update/` to nav.
- Structured lists live in `_data/` (`galleries.yml`, `documents.yml`, CSVs). Pages loop that data.
- Every HTML page needs `permalink: /slug/`. Asset URLs use `relative_url`.
- Photos: PhotoPrism at `https://photos.tlblazers.com`. This repo stores **pages and share tokens**, not the photo library.

## Do not

- Add plugins GitHub Pages will not build.
- Treat this as an AL app or invent AL-Go process.
- Force-push `main`.
